@wirybeaver thanks for cherry-picking the fix and preserving authorship in `7602fbeb`. Its full tree matches the previously CPU-checked `79dcd182`; I have not rerun or qualified GPU E2E on it.

One new current-main compatibility blocker: [Lint job 101839077491](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34153043250/job/101839077491) fails only `check-registered-tests`, because `test/registered/cp/test_flashinfer_prefill_cp.py` is outside `test/registered/<kind>/<subsystem>/`. I checked the [validator used by the CI merge ref](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/128cb3ff221a37e4258a8be70e892fc668fc5199/scripts/lint/check_registered_tests.py). A path-only move to `test/registered/e2e/cp/test_flashinfer_prefill_cp.py` looks appropriate for this server test, preserving its body, `base-b`/`2-gpu-large` registration and all assertions; the PR body's run command would also need updating. This is a proposed next fix, not a tested relocation.

Separately, the [base GPU gate](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34153043719/job/101839163267) explicitly stops because the PR is draft; skipped GPU jobs are not runtime failures or passes. No branch/CI-gate changes from me. This inspection is AI-assisted.

